# "At the beginning of combat on each player's turn, that player may draw a card. If they do, they can't attack this turn
# and you put a peace counter on this enchantment." (CR 507.1, 608.2c, 611.2c.) Bot1 draws at the beginning of combat of
# each of its turns, so on turn 3 the untapped, no longer summoning-sick Ornithopter cannot attack: the declaration is not
# even asked for. Each draw puts a peace counter on the enchantment.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Peace in Our Time
Ornithopter
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Peace in Our Time.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Attackers]
! Bot1.Attack
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Peace in Our Time.Counters.Peace = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot2.Life = 20
